Now main.js. This is the biggest. Need carefully implement.

Let's define constants:
```
const ACTIVE = {4:[2,3,4,5],6:[1,2,3,4,5,6],8:[0..7]};
const KEYMAP = {KeyA:0,...,Semicolon:7};
const KEYNAME = ['A','S','D','F','J','K','L',';'];
const WINDOWS = [0.045,0.09,0.135,0.18];
const SCORE = {perfect:3000,great:2000,good:1000,bad:300};
const WEIGHT = {perfect:1,great:.85,good:.55,bad:.25,miss:0};
```
Game vars:
```
let game = null;
let scene, audio, notes=[], pendingIndex=0;
let stats={...};
let lastSection=null;
let state='boot';
let holdLane = new Array(8).fill(null);
let held = new Array(8).fill(false);
let missTimer? 
```
Build note visuals after chart loaded.

`resetGame()`:
- for each note: state pending, group.visible false, head.visible true, body/tail visible type hold, scale reset, position.
- stats reset, combo 0, score 0, health 100, judged 0, weight 0, counts.
- note cursor 0.
- currentSection = 0; call updateSection(0,force).
- UI score etc.
- judge hide.
- pads states.
- scene maybe reset effects? Add scene.reset? Not implemented. Particles fade; okay.
- set all note group visible false.
- state playing.
- start audio.

`startSession()`:
```
if (!audio.loaded) return;
hide start/results/pause; hud show; reset; audio.start(0); state='playing'; toast('GET READY');
```
Need start audio context on click. `await audio.start()`.
Potential delay: audio start at ctx.currentTime+0.12; audio.time negative .12. Good.
- music starts at 0 with ~2.5s intro; first note 3.535.

`updateGame(dt)`:
```
const t=audio.time;
const sec = sectionAt(t);
if(sec!==lastSec){...}
scene.noteSpeed maybe constant.
for notes: updateNote(note,t)
update HUD each frame
if(t>=END){finish()}
```
Notes update every frame 331 * fine.

Visibility:
```
function updateNote(n,t){
  const y=(n.data.t-t)*SPEED;
  const dur=n.data.dur||0;
  if (n.state==='pending') {
    const endY=y; // head
    n.group.position.set(scene.laneX(n.lane), y, scene.laneZ(n.lane)+0.2);
    const show = y < 13.5 && y > -0.4; // note above
    // for holds body extends above; if y < 0 and not hit, still falling; show until miss
    n.group.visible = y < 13.5 && y > -1.2;
    n.head.visible=true;
    if (n.body) {
      const len = dur*SPEED;
      n.body.scale.set(0.42,len,1);
      n.body.position.y=len/2; // local
      n.tail.position.y=len;
      n.body.visible = true; n.tail.visible = true;
    }
    if (t > n.data.t + 0.185) missNote(n);
  } else if (n.state==='holding') {
    n.group.visible=true;
    n.group.position.set(scene.laneX(n.lane), 0.02, scene.laneZ(n.lane)+0.2);
    n.head.visible=false;
    const remain=Math.max(0,(n.endTime-t))*SPEED;
    if (n.body) { n.body.visible=remain>0.02; n.body.scale.set(0.42, remain,1); n.body.position.y=remain/2; n.tail.position.y=remain; n.tail.visible=remain>0.3; }
    if (t >= n.endTime - .02) completeHold(n);
  } else { n.group.visible=false; }
}
```
For holds, group at head y; body local y from 0 to len, good. When holding, group at y=0; body 0..remain. Tail at remain. Head hidden.
But if note passes ring and is pending, y<0, body tail still above; group visible until y>-1.2. If miss at y=-1.5, then hide.

Holding body color maybe white flash. fine.

End time for hold: data.t + data.dur.

HUD note: Score display.

pressLane:
```
function pressLane(lane){
 if(state!=='playing') return;
 scene.pressFx(lane); audio.click(lane,.35);
 if(audio.time<0) return;
 // find best pending note in lane
 let best=null, bestAbs=1e9;
 for (const n of notes) { if(n.lane!==lane||n.state!=='pending') continue; const d=audio.time-n.data.t; if(d<-0.16||d>0.185) continue; const a=Math.abs(d); if(a<bestAbs){...}}
 if(!best) return;
 judgeHit(best, audio.time-best.data.t)
}
```
Scanning all notes per press is fine. Could limit with cursor but not necessary.

Judge:
```
const q = abs<=.045?'perfect':abs<=.09?'great':abs<=.135?'good':'bad';
if(q==='bad') break combo? Standard bad breaks combo; yes.
...
n.state = type hold? 'holding':'done';
n.head.visible=false;
if hold set holdLane[lane]=n; endTime...
stats.counts[q]++; stats.judged++; stats.weight += WEIGHT[q]; stats.score += SCORE[q]; stats.combo++ if q !== 'bad'? 
```
Hmm combo increments on all hits including bad? Typical bad breaks. Use if perfect/great/good -> combo++; bad -> combo=0. Miss -> 0.
- For perfect/great/good, combo++; maxCombo update.
- score adds.
- health.
- judgement text; scene.hitFx; audio.click.
- For holds, note.completed=false; note.holdTicks=0; head hidden; body visible. Show "HOLD" maybe not.

`showJudge(q,text?)`: set class and text; restart animation by removing class, void offsetWidth, add class. For combo bump.

`missNote(n)`:
- Only if pending. n.state='miss'; n.group.visible=false; stats.miss++; stats.judged++; stats.weight +=0; combo=0; health-=5; scene.missFx(lane); audio.thud(); showJudge('miss','MISS').
- If n.type hold, its entire hold missed. Good.
- For inactive lane notes? chart only active; transitions.

`completeHold(n)`:
- if state holding: state done; hide group; holdLane[lane]=null; score+=400; health+=1; show "HOLD" maybe; scene.hitFx? maybe smaller; spawn? call scene.pressFx. Add not judged (head already). Combo? Keep. Maybe combo++ to reward? That inflates max combo beyond note count; avoid. Keep.
- If reached end while key still held, complete automatically. Mark `held` remains; next hold can start on same lane while key held? If player holds key through next hold onset, press already happened, so no new hit. That's standard: need re-press. Fine.

`dropHold(n)`:
- state dropped; stats.miss++; stats.judged++; stats.weight+=0; combo=0; health-=4; hide; showJudge('miss','HOLD LOST'); audio.thud.
- But the head was already judged and counted; adding another judged makes accuracy lower (appropriate). Max combo count maybe. Fine.

Hold ticks:
- In loop, for each lane if holdLane[lane] and held[lane]: accumulate `holdTickTimer`; every 0.1s score += 20, health += .05. Not essential for accuracy. Could skip ticks for simplicity. But hold feedback nice: body animates. Score completion enough. Keep simple: no ticks. Yet user expects hold; we can add score tick with timer. Add `n.tickAt` and while t > tickAt && t < end: score+=25; tickAt+=0.12; small flash every 3 ticks? Could be too much. Do score only.

Release:
```
function releaseLane(lane){ 
  scene...; held[lane]=false;
  const n=holdLane[lane]; if(!n) return;
  holdLane[lane]=null;
  if(audio.time < n.endTime - 0.12) dropHold(n); else completeHold(n);
}
```
