content.text:
Now main.js. Add BEST storage and DOM refs. Let me view relevant top lines and finishGame.

Add constants after END_TIME:
```js
const BEST_KEY = 'cryout-best-v1';
```

DOM add `bestScoreLabel`, `bestBadge`, `bestNote`.

Add functions after stats maybe:

```js
function readBest() {
  try {
    const raw = localStorage.getItem(BEST_KEY);
    if (!raw) return null;
    const b = JSON.parse(raw);
    if (!b || typeof b.score !== 'number') return null;
    return b;
  } catch { return null; }
}
let personalBest = readBest();

function renderBest() {
  const label = dom.bestScoreLabel;
  if (label) {
    label.textContent = personalBest
      ? `${String(personalBest.score).padStart(7,'0')} · ${personalBest.rank}`
      : '—';
  }
}
```

At load (after dom defined), call renderBest() — but personalBest declared before dom? I can declare after dom refs. Order:
- constants
- dom
- state
- best functions (uses dom)
- `let personalBest = readBest();` and `renderBest();` after function definitions, but must be after dom exists (yes) and before buildNotes? Fine.

In finishGame after computing acc/rank/full:
```js
const score = stats.score;
const prevBest = personalBest;
const isBest = !personalBest || score > personalBest.score ||
  (score === personalBest.score && acc > (personalBest.acc ?? 0));
if (isBest) {
  personalBest = { score, acc, rank, maxCombo: stats.maxCombo, full, at: Date.now() };
  try { localStorage.setItem(BEST_KEY, JSON.stringify(personalBest)); } catch {}
}
dom.bestBadge.classList.toggle('on', isBest);
dom.bestNote.innerHTML = personalBest
  ? `BEST <b>${String(personalBest.score).padStart(7,'0')}</b> · ${personalBest.rank} · ${personalBest.acc.toFixed(2)}%`
  : '';
renderBest();
```

Careful: innerHTML with values we control (numbers/rank) safe. But better use textContent pieces. Simpler: `dom.bestNote.textContent = 'BEST ' + ...`. Then no bold. We have .best-note b CSS unused. Could build with spans safely:
```js
dom.bestNote.innerHTML = `BEST <b>${...}</b> · ...`
```
Values numeric/rank from internal, safe. Fine.

Also when returning to menu and replaying, badge should not persist from last results? `finishGame` toggles each time. Start screen doesn't show badge. fine.

In `quitToMenu`, maybe hide bestBadge? It's inside results hidden; no issue.

`retryGame` hides result then startGame; badge class remains until next finish; harmless.

Expose `personalBest` getter:
```js
get best() { return personalBest; }
```
Not necessary but tests.

Also localStorage loaded once at module init; if user has old data, display.

What if localStorage access throws (privacy)? readBest catches. write catches.

Add `renderBest();` call after buildNotes/resetGame.

Let's implement.

